  "tagline": "MySQL-compatible SQL database you can branch, diff, merge and clone like a Git repository.",
  "description": "Dolt is a SQL database with Git semantics built in: every write lands in a commit graph, so you can branch, diff, merge, revert and push/pull tables between remotes using SQL procedures or a Git-like CLI. It speaks the MySQL wire protocol and dialect, stores data in prolly trees that make diffs and structural sharing cheap, and since 2.0 (2026) runs automatic garbage collection and compressed archive storage by default. DoltHub also offers DoltHub/DoltLab for collaboration, Hosted Dolt, and Doltgres, a PostgreSQL-flavored sibling. It fits data that needs review workflows and auditability, not raw OLTP throughput.",
